## The exact delta (from `diff -u` between the two Ruby steps)

`@week1_baseline/ruby/00_config/lib/boukensha/config.rb` →
`@week1_baseline/ruby/01_struct_skeleton/lib/boukensha/config.rb`:
- drops `require "bundler/setup"` (no Python equivalent needed — nothing to
  port, Python has no Bundler concept)
- drops the `PROMPTS_DIR` constant entirely

`@week1_baseline/ruby/00_config/lib/boukensha/tasks/base.rb` and
`.../tasks/player.rb` → unchanged, byte-identical.

`@week1_baseline/ruby/00_config/lib/boukensha.rb` →
`@week1_baseline/ruby/01_struct_skeleton/lib/boukensha.rb`: adds three new
`require_relative`s — `boukensha/tool`, `boukensha/message`,
`boukensha/context`.

`@week1_baseline/ruby/00_config/examples/example.rb` →
`@week1_baseline/ruby/01_struct_skeleton/examples/example.rb`: rewritten.
Still builds a `Config` and resolves `player_settings`/`system_prompt`, but
`system_prompt` is now called with **only** `user_prompts_dir:` (no
`default_prompts_dir:` — consistent with `PROMPTS_DIR` being dropped). The
rest of the script now builds a `Context`, registers one `move` `Tool`, seeds
two `Message`s via `add_message`, and prints four sections (`Config:`,
`Context:`, `Tool:`, `Messages:`) instead of the old six-field config dump.

